G2 PROMPTS + SCHEMAS (design calls reported)
- Format decision: Markdown + YAML front-matter. Rationale: human-reviewable in the
  repo, version pinned in filename AND front-matter, parseable with a stdlib-only
  split (no new dependency, no network).
- backend/app/services/providers/prompts/extract-food-v1.md +
  extract-medicine-v1.md: versioned files; system instruction carries the
  provider-neutral rule "never infer beyond visible evidence".
- backend/app/services/providers/schemas.py (Pydantic v2, sync, extra=forbid):
  ExtractionItem (name, expiry_date YYYY-MM-DD, date_type, confidence 0..1,
  uncertainty_reasons required when confidence<1.0); ExtractionOutput (items,
  unknowns REQUIRED, needs_evidence; needs_evidence=>unknowns non-empty;
  unknowns entries must be items.<i>.<field> pointing at a null field —
  fabricated values fail). parse_extraction_output: prose/wrong-types fail as
  ValidationError (single exception type, prose never parsed).
- Repair: extract_with_single_repair(supply) — exactly ONE retry on first-attempt
  invalid_json ProviderError or ValidationError, then ExtractionFailedError.
  NO new extraction.py: quoted reason — the helper is pure validation logic over
  in-memory payloads (no I/O, no provider wiring, no reader); a second module would
  add import surface with no caller. SG-028 owns the production reader.

